title: 'pallet-broker: fix double counting when re-pooling an active region'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    Fixes ways a region could be counted twice in the instantaneous pool.

    Re-pooling or assigning a region that has already started now removes its old pool entry.
    Revenue can no longer be claimed while a region is pooled provisionally, as a claim moves
    the pool entry and re-pooling afterwards would miss it. When a started region is re-pooled
    or assigned, revenue for the timeslices that already passed stays claimable.
crates:
- name: pallet-broker
  bump: major
